    "review::.::holistic::cross_module_architecture::sqlite_persistence_duplication": {
      "id": "review::.::holistic::cross_module_architecture::sqlite_persistence_duplication",
      "detector": "review",
      "file": ".",
      "tier": 1,
      "confidence": "high",
      "summary": "Five crates independently implement identical SQLite open/schema/default-path boilerplate with no shared persistence substrate",
      "detail": {
        "holistic": true,
        "dimension": "cross_module_architecture",
        "related_files": [
          "crates/colony-agent/src/persistence.rs",
          "crates/colony-focus/src/persistence.rs",
          "crates/colony-reflection/src/storage.rs",
          "crates/colony-secure/src/approvals.rs",
          "crates/colony-tuple/src/persistent.rs"
        ],
        "evidence": [
          "All five files implement the same open(path)/open_default()/open_in_memory() constructor triad",
          "All five wrap Connection in Mutex<Connection> for synchronization with identical lock-poisoning error messages",
          "All five call create_dir_all on the parent directory with nearly identical patterns before opening",
          "colony-agent uses AgentError::Conversation to wrap rusqlite::Error; colony-focus uses FocusError::Database; colony-reflection defines StorageError with #[from] rusqlite::Error; colony-secure unwraps rusqlite directly through its own Result alias \u2014 four incompatible error wrapping conventions for the same underlying operation",
          "Path conventions diverge: colony-agent and colony-focus use dirs::config_dir().join('colony'), while colony-reflection uses dirs::home_dir().join('.colony'), producing different filesystem locations on some platforms"
        ],
        "suggestion": "Extract a colony-storage crate (or a storage module in colony-config) providing: a SqliteStore builder with open/open_default/open_in_memory, a uniform StorageError wrapping rusqlite::Error, and a single colony_data_dir() function that all crates call for the canonical ~/.colony/ path. Each existing store becomes a thin domain wrapper around this substrate. This eliminates the config_dir vs home_dir divergence and centralises rusqlite version negotiation.",
        "reasoning": "",
        "content_hash": "3b34d451"
      },
      "status": "open",
      "note": null,
      "first_seen": "2026-03-12T21:19:33+00:00",
