    "review::.::holistic::logic_clarity::reconnect_state_on_failure": {
      "id": "review::.::holistic::logic_clarity::reconnect_state_on_failure",
      "detector": "review",
      "file": ".",
      "tier": 1,
      "confidence": "high",
      "summary": "McpConnection::reconnect sets state to Reconnecting after a failed reconnect attempt instead of retaining the failure state",
      "detail": {
        "holistic": true,
        "dimension": "logic_clarity",
        "related_files": [
          "crates/colony-mcp/src/connection.rs"
        ],
        "evidence": [
          "Lines 270-278: when self.connect() fails, the Err branch logs the error and then sets `self.state = ConnectionState::Reconnecting` (line 276) before returning Err. At the time of return the connection is not reconnecting \u2014 it has failed.",
          "Callers observing the connection state after a failed reconnect will see Reconnecting, which implies an active background process, not a terminal failure for this attempt.",
          "By contrast, the success path (line 264) correctly sets nothing (connect() already sets state=Connected internally). The failure path should either leave state as Disconnected (set by disconnect() called on line 260) or set it to Failed."
        ],
        "suggestion": "Remove the `self.state = ConnectionState::Reconnecting;` assignment from the Err branch (line 276). The state was already set to Disconnected by the preceding `self.disconnect().await` call, which is the accurate state after a failed reconnect attempt. If a persistent 'reconnect in progress' state is needed, that signal belongs at the pool level, not within the failed connection.",
        "reasoning": "",
        "content_hash": "d3dfcb96"
      },
      "status": "open",
      "note": null,
      "first_seen": "2026-03-12T21:19:33+00:00",
