      "id": "review::.::holistic::logic_clarity::nested_iflet_maybe_decrypt",
      "detector": "review",
      "file": ".",
      "tier": 1,
      "confidence": "high",
      "summary": "maybe_decrypt_value uses three-level nested conditionals where a combinator chain would be clearer",
      "detail": {
        "holistic": true,
        "dimension": "logic_clarity",
        "related_files": [
          "crates/colony-expand/src/context.rs"
        ],
        "evidence": [
          "Lines 37-44: `if is_encrypted { if let Some(key) = get_cached_secure_key() { if let Ok(decrypted) = decrypt(..) { return decrypted; } } }`. Three levels of nesting for a try-decrypt-else-passthrough operation.",
          "Project RUST_STYLE_GUIDE.md explicitly prohibits nested if-let: 'Nested if let is Always Wrong. If you write if let inside another if let, stop and refactor.'",
          "The decryption check can be expressed as a combinator: `is_encrypted(&value).then(|| get_cached_secure_key()?.and_then(|key| decrypt(&value, key).ok())).flatten().unwrap_or(value)` or via let-else."
        ],
        "suggestion": "Flatten using let-else: `if !colony_secure::is_encrypted(&value) { return value; }; let Some(key) = get_cached_secure_key() else { return value; }; colony_secure::decrypt(&value, key).unwrap_or(value)`. This makes each guard a single exit point and matches the project's stated style.",
        "reasoning": "",
        "content_hash": "47cbfae3"
      },
      "status": "open",
      "note": null,
      "first_seen": "2026-03-12T21:19:33+00:00",
      "last_seen": "2026-03-12T21:19:53+00:00",
      "resolved_at": null,
      "reopen_count": 0,
      "lang": "rust",
      "suppressed": false,
      "suppressed_at": null,
      "suppression_pattern": null
    },
    "review::.::holistic::logic_clarity::nested_iflet_nameref_resolution": {
      "id": "review::.::holistic::logic_clarity::nested_iflet_nameref_resolution",
      "detector": "review",
      "file": ".",
      "tier": 1,
      "confidence": "high",
      "summary": "get_var_or_env_raw NameRef branch uses a four-level nested if-let pyramid in violation of project style guide",
      "detail": {
        "holistic": true,
        "dimension": "logic_clarity",
        "related_files": [
          "crates/colony-expand/src/context.rs"
        ],
        "evidence": [
          "Lines 1176-1184: `if let Some(var) = self.variables.get(name) { if let Variable::NameRef(_target) = var { if let Some(resolved) = self.resolve_nameref(name) { if let Some(target_var) = self.variables.get(&resolved) { return ...; } return ...; } return None; } return ...; }`. Four nesting levels.",
          "The same NameRef resolution logic appears in get_variable (lines 1007-1013) and set_variable (lines 1256-1261) using a more direct pattern. The get_var_or_env_raw version is the most convoluted.",
          "Project style guide: 'No exceptions. If you think you need nested if let, you don't.'"
        ],
        "suggestion": "Refactor using let-else at each decision point: `let Some(var) = self.variables.get(name) else { return self.environment.get(name).cloned(); }; if !matches!(var, Variable::NameRef(_)) { return Some(var.as_str().to_string()); }; let Some(resolved) = self.resolve_nameref(name) else { return None; }; if let Some(target_var) = self.variables.get(&resolved) { return Some(target_var.as_str().to_string()); }; return self.environment.get(&resolved).cloned();`",
        "reasoning": "",
        "content_hash": "62305bd5"
      },
      "status": "open",
      "note": null,
      "first_seen": "2026-03-12T21:19:33+00:00",
      "last_seen": "2026-03-12T21:19:53+00:00",
      "resolved_at": null,
      "reopen_count": 0,
      "lang": "rust",
      "suppressed": false,
      "suppressed_at": null,
      "suppression_pattern": null
    },
