      "detector": "review",
      "file": ".",
      "tier": 1,
      "confidence": "high",
      "summary": "Timestamp fields typed as String carry ISO-8601 semantic contracts not enforced by the type",
      "detail": {
        "holistic": true,
        "dimension": "type_safety",
        "related_files": [
          "crates/colony-recipe/src/registry.rs",
          "crates/colony-exec/src/goals/types.rs"
        ],
        "evidence": [
          "InstalledRecipe::installed_at: String (registry.rs:20) \u2014 populated by callers with RFC-3339 strings but nothing prevents arbitrary non-date strings",
          "Goal::created_at: String, updated_at: String (goals/types.rs:53-55) \u2014 set via chrono::Utc::now().to_rfc3339() but stored and compared as bare strings throughout the tree"
        ],
        "suggestion": "Replace String timestamp fields with chrono::DateTime<Utc>; serde's built-in support handles serialization. This makes the contract machine-verifiable and eliminates silent format mismatches.",
