        "dimension": "api_surface_coherence",
        "related_files": [
          "crates/colony-agent/src/agent.rs"
        ],
        "evidence": [
          "process() at line 353 builds a completion stream, wraps it in cancellable_stream, and collects text \u2014 tool events in the stream are silently dropped by the StreamEvent::_ arm in cancellable_stream",
          "process_full() at line 476 performs explicit stream polling including StreamEvent::ToolCallStart and StreamEvent::ToolCallComplete dispatch to handle_tool_use()",
          "The name 'full' communicates the difference only loosely; there is no type-level distinction (both return Result<String>) and no doc comment on process() warning that tool calls are not executed",
          "A caller choosing process() for an agent configured with tools will silently receive no tool execution"
        ],
        "suggestion": "Either merge into a single process() that always handles tool calls (making tool handling the default, not opt-in), or introduce a type-level distinction such as returning a ProcessHandle enum so callers cannot accidentally choose the wrong mode. At minimum, add a doc comment on process() that explicitly states tool calls are ignored.",
        "reasoning": "",
