      "detail": {
        "holistic": true,
        "dimension": "error_consistency",
        "related_files": [
          "crates/colony-secure/src/approvals.rs"
        ],
        "evidence": [
          "Lines 162-164 and 204-206: DateTime::parse_from_rfc3339(&granted_at_str).map(|dt| dt.with_timezone(&Utc)).unwrap_or_else(|_| Utc::now()) \u2014 a parse failure silently substitutes the current time",
          "This pattern appears identically in both list_approvals() and list_all_approvals()",
          "In a security-audit context (approval records for sensitive variable access), silently replacing a corrupt timestamp with the current time produces misleading results with no diagnostic"
        ],
        "suggestion": "Propagate the parse error instead: use DateTime::parse_from_rfc3339(&granted_at_str).map_err(|e| rusqlite::Error::FromSqlConversionFailure(4, rusqlite::types::Type::Text, Box::new(e)))? inside the query_map closure, or define a SecureError variant for database integrity failures and use map_err(|_| SecureError::CorruptTimestamp(granted_at_str.clone())). At minimum, log a warning with the raw value before substituting.",
