    "review::.::holistic::mid_level_elegance::agent_dual_process_paths": {
      "id": "review::.::holistic::mid_level_elegance::agent_dual_process_paths",
      "detector": "review",
      "file": ".",
      "tier": 1,
      "confidence": "high",
      "summary": "Agent.process() and Agent.process_full() implement the same loop independently with diverged accounting, persistence, and observation logic",
      "detail": {
        "holistic": true,
        "dimension": "mid_level_elegance",
        "related_files": [
          "crates/colony-agent/src/agent.rs"
        ],
        "evidence": [
          "process() records token usage via token_tracker.record() and saves messages to ConversationStore; process_full() skips token accounting and ConversationStore persistence entirely.",
          "process_full() emits a ReflectionObserver observation at the end; process() does not.",
          "Both methods clone messages, build a CompletionRequest, and push an assistant response \u2014 identical orchestration logic copied rather than shared.",
          "process() delegates to cancellable_stream (a clean composable abstraction); process_full() drives the stream directly with while-let, duplicating the Done/Error/TextDelta handling."
        ],
        "suggestion": "Extract a private async fn run_completion_loop(&mut self, request: CompletionRequest, cancel: &CancellationToken) -> Result<String> that drives the stream and returns the full response text. Both process_with_cancellation() and process_full() call this shared core, then apply their own post-processing (token accounting, persistence, observation) in one place. This eliminates the risk of one path receiving a fix that the other silently misses.",
        "reasoning": "",
        "content_hash": "38a531bd"
      },
      "status": "open",
      "note": null,
      "first_seen": "2026-03-12T21:19:33+00:00",
      "last_seen": "2026-03-12T21:19:53+00:00",
      "resolved_at": null,
      "reopen_count": 0,
      "lang": "rust",
      "suppressed": false,
      "suppressed_at": null,
      "suppression_pattern": null
    },
    "review::.::holistic::mid_level_elegance::tool_result_fake_user_message": {
      "id": "review::.::holistic::mid_level_elegance::tool_result_fake_user_message",
      "detector": "review",
      "file": ".",
      "tier": 1,
      "confidence": "high",
      "summary": "Tool results are injected into message history as MessageRole::User with a plain-text prefix, making user messages structurally ambiguous",
      "detail": {
        "holistic": true,
        "dimension": "mid_level_elegance",
        "related_files": [
          "crates/colony-agent/src/agent.rs"
        ],
        "evidence": [
          "agent.rs line 612-615: after tool execution, a Message { role: MessageRole::User, content: MessageContent::Text(format!(\"Tool result: {}\", result_str)) } is pushed to self.messages.",
          "Any consumer that iterates self.messages cannot distinguish genuine user turns from synthetic tool-result turns without string-prefix inspection.",
          "MessageContent already has a Blocks variant with ContentBlock::ToolResult; the provider layer understands this variant but it is not used here."
        ],
        "suggestion": "Use MessageContent::Blocks with a ContentBlock::ToolResult { tool_use_id, content } block to inject tool results. This keeps the message history structurally honest: consumers can match on role and content type without parsing text. The MessageRole should be User only for genuine user input; a distinct content type communicates the tool-result semantic without requiring a custom role.",
        "reasoning": "",
        "content_hash": "48ef332c"
      },
      "status": "open",
      "note": null,
      "first_seen": "2026-03-12T21:19:33+00:00",
      "last_seen": "2026-03-12T21:19:53+00:00",
      "resolved_at": null,
      "reopen_count": 0,
      "lang": "rust",
      "suppressed": false,
      "suppressed_at": null,
      "suppression_pattern": null
    },
    "review::.::holistic::mid_level_elegance::agent_definition_translation_duplicated": {
      "id": "review::.::holistic::mid_level_elegance::agent_definition_translation_duplicated",
      "detector": "review",
      "file": ".",
      "tier": 1,
      "confidence": "high",
      "summary": "AgentDefinition-to-AgentConfig translation logic is duplicated between from_definition() and configure_from_definition() with diverging control flow",
      "detail": {
        "holistic": true,
        "dimension": "mid_level_elegance",
        "related_files": [
          "crates/colony-agent/src/agent.rs"
        ],
        "evidence": [
          "Both from_definition() (lines 109-137) and configure_from_definition() (lines 140-183) contain the same model-spec parsing: split_once(':'), ProviderType::parse, infer_provider_from_model fallback.",
          "from_definition() uses early-return Ok(Self::with_provider(...)) when a provider is parsed; configure_from_definition() uses let-binding with unwrap_or_else and calls switch_model separately.",
          "configure_from_definition() checks temperature with is_some() before assigning, while from_definition() assigns unconditionally \u2014 a subtle behavioral difference that is not documented."
        ],
        "suggestion": "Extract fn apply_definition_to_config(definition: &AgentDefinition, config: &mut AgentConfig) -> Option<(ProviderType, String)> that applies all scalar fields and returns the parsed provider+model if present. Both from_definition() and configure_from_definition() call this helper, then each handles provider instantiation in its own way. This puts the translation in exactly one place.",
        "reasoning": "",
        "content_hash": "9fe8995f"
      },
      "status": "open",
      "note": null,
      "first_seen": "2026-03-12T21:19:33+00:00",
      "last_seen": "2026-03-12T21:19:53+00:00",
      "resolved_at": null,
      "reopen_count": 0,
      "lang": "rust",
      "suppressed": false,
