      "suppression_pattern": null
    },
    "review::.::holistic::mid_level_elegance::docker_status_bypasses_subscription_boundary": {
      "id": "review::.::holistic::mid_level_elegance::docker_status_bypasses_subscription_boundary",
      "detector": "review",
      "file": ".",
      "tier": 1,
      "confidence": "high",
      "summary": "DockerStatusComponent spawns a synchronous subprocess in render() instead of using the subscription/tuple mechanism, breaking the reactive boundary contract",
      "detail": {
        "holistic": true,
        "dimension": "mid_level_elegance",
        "related_files": [
          "crates/colony-ui-core/src/builtins/docker_status.rs"
        ],
        "evidence": [
          "DockerStatusComponent::render() calls std::process::Command::new(\"docker\").args([\"ps\",\"-q\"]).output() synchronously on every render invocation.",
          "subscriptions() returns vec![] \u2014 the component declares no reactive dependencies, so the cache-invalidation mechanism cannot gate re-renders.",
          "Every other builtin prompt component reads from the ComponentContext passed at the boundary (env vars, job counts, last_exit_code) without side-effectful I/O; docker_status is the only one that reaches outside the boundary."
        ],
        "suggestion": "Either (a) have a background poller emit a docker_status tuple to TupleSpace when container count changes, subscribe via subscriptions() to that pattern, and read the count from ComponentContext data rather than invoking docker at render time; or (b) add a poll_interval() override (e.g. 5 seconds) so the framework controls re-render frequency and make the I/O explicit. The key fix is that the render boundary should not perform blocking I/O that bypasses the subscription contract.",
        "reasoning": "",
        "content_hash": "821fa3a1"
      },
      "status": "open",
      "note": null,
      "first_seen": "2026-03-12T21:19:33+00:00",
      "last_seen": "2026-03-12T21:19:53+00:00",
      "resolved_at": null,
      "reopen_count": 0,
      "lang": "rust",
      "suppressed": false,
      "suppressed_at": null,
      "suppression_pattern": null
    },
    "review::.::holistic::mid_level_elegance::sidebar_builtin_inline_glue": {
      "id": "review::.::holistic::mid_level_elegance::sidebar_builtin_inline_glue",
      "detector": "review",
      "file": ".",
      "tier": 1,
      "confidence": "high",
      "summary": "The 'sidebar' builtin in execute_builtin() is handled inline with a direct TupleSpace.out() call rather than through the dispatch pattern used by all other builtins",
      "detail": {
        "holistic": true,
        "dimension": "mid_level_elegance",
        "related_files": [
          "crates/colony-exec/src/builtins.rs"
        ],
        "evidence": [
          "Lines 281-296 in the builtin match arm for 'sidebar': parse_sidebar_args is called, then serde_json::to_string and tuple_space.out() are invoked inline, bypassing the function-per-builtin pattern used by every other handler.",
          "All other builtins (cd, export, flux, mirror, pane, etc.) are dispatched to a dedicated function: builtin_cd(), crate::flux::builtin_flux(), crate::panes::builtin_split(), etc.",
          "The inline branch also calls unwrap_or_default() on the JSON serialization, silently swallowing serialization errors that would be surfaced as Err() in a dedicated function."
        ],
        "suggestion": "Move the sidebar logic into crate::sidebar::builtin_sidebar(&args, tuple_space) following the existing pattern, and replace the inline branch with a single dispatch call. This keeps the execute_builtin() dispatch table uniform and surfaces serialization errors through the Result<BuiltinResult> return type.",
        "reasoning": "",
        "content_hash": "1b0c2272"
      },
      "status": "open",
      "note": null,
      "first_seen": "2026-03-12T21:19:33+00:00",
      "last_seen": "2026-03-12T21:19:53+00:00",
      "resolved_at": null,
      "reopen_count": 0,
      "lang": "rust",
      "suppressed": false,
